  [34mdescription:[0m  During caco-web duty cycle 0118, a lightweight current-assets Playwright pass observed the first `/api/v1/ui/snapshot` request returning `502 Bad Gateway`. Chromium recorded it as a browser console error even though subsequent snapshot requests recovered with `200 OK` and the UI showed degraded snapshot copy.

Evidence:
- `.cacophony/agent/ms-mac-cacophony-caco-web/summary/0118/web/observation.log` around the `--- console` and `--- network` sections shows `Total messages: 1 (Errors: 1, Warnings: 0)` and `[GET] .../api/v1/ui/snapshot => [502] Bad Gateway`.
- `.cacophony/agent/ms-mac-cacophony-caco-web/summary/0118/web/console/console-2026-04-28T01-00-07-092Z.log` contains the Chromium console error: `Failed to load resource: the server responded with a status of 502 (Bad Gateway)`.
- `.cacophony/agent/ms-mac-cacophony-caco-web/summary/0118/web/server.log` shows request `GET /api/v1/ui/snapshot -> 502 5478ms`, followed by recovered `200` snapshot responses.

Expected: handled daemon/proxy restart or unreachable snapshot failures should be surfaced in caco-web UI state without producing browser-console resource errors, consistent with the existing bd-c2310e console-clean sentinel behavior for handled daemon 503/unavailable paths.

Actual: the proxy returns a raw 502 for `/api/v1/ui/snapshot`, which Chromium logs as a console error.
